{{- /*
  beads-issues/push-and-open-pr — headless (no mitto_ui_* calls) push +
  PR-create-or-update, safe to call exactly once from an automated loop
  driver's Done branch. Supports one PR per bead or one shared PR per epic.

  Called EXACTLY ONCE, inline in each driver's Done branch (e.g.
  loop-fixing-bug Step 3d, loop-implementing-feature Step 3e, mention-driver
  Step 3f) — never per phase. A feature bead crosses four phases in four
  separate turns; opening a PR per phase would spam four PRs for one bead.

  Composes git/shared/identify-remote-branch (resolves <target-remote> /
  <target-branch> / <push-remote>) and git/shared/behind-base-count
  (detection only — no interactive verdict fragment is pulled in, so nothing
  here prompts the user).

  Unlike git/shared/create-or-update-pr (built around mitto_ui_form +
  mitto_ui_textbox for title/description/reviewers), this fragment is
  headless-only by construction: the agent writes the title and body itself
  and reports the URL back onto the bead as a comment instead of presenting
  a form. Both paths share git/shared/pr-description-no-beads, which also
  bans `--fill` (driver commits carry `(refs <bead-id>)` footers).

  Callers pass a dict:
    "Ctx"    — the full render context (`.`), forwarded verbatim to the
               nested identify-remote-branch / behind-base-count calls.
    "Target" — the resolved bead ID. Required; the PR URL is commented here.

  Preconditions: the working tree is clean (everything already committed)
  and the caller is already on the bead's feature branch (usually via
  beads-issues/shared/ensure-bead-branch).
*/ -}}
{{- $ctx := .Ctx -}}
{{- $target := .Target -}}
{{- $fromBranch := Default "main" $ctx.Args.FromBranch -}}
{{- $groupEpics := ne $ctx.Args.GroupEpics "false" -}}
{{ template "git/shared/identify-remote-branch" $ctx }}

For this workflow, set `<target-branch>` to the explicit base
`{{ $fromBranch }}`. Resolve the PR owner before continuing:

```bash
pr_target="{{ $target }}"
grouped_epic=false
{{ if $groupEpics -}}
parent=$(bd show {{ $target }} --json | jq -r '.[0].parent // empty')
if [ -n "$parent" ] && [ "$(bd show "$parent" --json | jq -r '.[0].issue_type // empty')" = "epic" ]; then
  pr_target="$parent"
  grouped_epic=true
fi
{{- end }}
```

{{ if $groupEpics -}}
When `grouped_epic=true`, count the epic's other open children, excluding
`{{ $target }}` (the caller closes this child immediately after this fragment).
If any remain, do **not** run the push/PR subsections below. Comment on the child
that its commit is on the shared epic branch and the PR is deferred until the
last child, then return to the caller's close step. This is what guarantees one
PR for the whole epic rather than one per child.

```bash
if [ "$grouped_epic" = true ]; then
  open_others=$(bd children "$pr_target" --json | jq --arg id "{{ $target }}" \
    '[.[] | select(.id != $id and .status != "closed")] | length')
  if [ "$open_others" -gt 0 ]; then
    bd comment {{ $target }} "Committed to shared epic branch; PR deferred until the epic's last open child finishes."
    # Skip the remaining PR subsections and return to the caller's close step.
  fi
fi
```
{{- end }}

#### Preflight: not behind the base

{{ template "git/shared/behind-base-count" $ctx }}

If behind (`> 0`), do **not** push: `bd comment {{ $target }}` explaining the
branch is `<N>` commits behind `<target-remote>/<target-branch>` and needs a
rebase first, then stop — do not open or update a PR against a stale base.

#### Push and create-or-update the PR

{{ template "git/shared/pr-description-no-beads" $ctx }}

This bead is being submitted by an automated driver, so there is no user to
review the wording — compose the title and body yourself from the branch's
diff and commits, stripping every bead reference. When `grouped_epic=true`,
title the PR for the epic and summarize all completed children represented by
the shared branch, not only the final child.

Idempotent — check for an existing PR before creating a new one:

```bash
existing_url=$(gh pr view <branch-name> --json url,state -q '.url' 2>/dev/null)
if [ -n "$existing_url" ]; then
  git push <push-remote> <branch-name>
  pr_url="$existing_url"
else
  git push -u <push-remote> <branch-name>
  gh pr create --title "<title>" --body-file <path> --base {{ $fromBranch | printf "%q" }}   # GitHub
  # glab mr create --title "<title>" --description "<body>"                   # GitLab
  pr_url=$(gh pr view <branch-name> --json url -q '.url')
fi
```

#### Report back

```bash
bd comment "$pr_target" "PR: $pr_url"
if [ "$pr_target" != "{{ $target }}" ]; then bd comment {{ $target }} "Epic PR: $pr_url"; fi
```

No `mitto_ui_*` calls anywhere in this fragment — safe for unattended runs.
{{- /* no trailing newline */ -}}
